  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Suppose that \\(f(x + 3) = 3x^2 + 7x + 4\\) and \\(f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.\\) What is \\(a + b + c?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Evaluating \\(f(x)=ax^2+bx+c\\) at \\(x=1\\) makes every power of \\(x\\) equal to \\(1\\), so\n\\[\nf(1)=a+b+c.\n\\]\nTo obtain \\(f(1)\\) from the given formula for \\(f(x+3)\\), choose \\(x=-2\\), since \\(-2+3=1\\). Then\n\\[\nf(1)=3(-2)^2+7(-2)+4\n=12-14+4=2.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(a+b+c=2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
